<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rambagh Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1835</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rambagh Palace is a former royal residence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaipur">Jaipur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>. Built in 1835 as a garden house and later enlarged into a palace, it became the main residence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> Man Singh II in 1925, and in 1957 it was converted into a luxury hotel, one of the first palace hotels in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and a model for the heritage tourism of Rajasthan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rambagh-palace.jpg" alt="Rambagh Palace" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chainwit. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rambagh_Palace_hotel_Jaipur_lobby_courtyard.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
